rl":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T22:21:09Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T15:24:28Z","body":"## Review checklist for @jncraton\n\n### AI usage\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS AI policy](https://joss.theoj.org/about#ai-policy) and understand that:\n  - AI may only be used for **non-substantive assistance** (e.g., grammar checking my review text, contextualizing public materials)\n  - **All evaluative decisions**—including scoring, accept/reject recommendations, and assessments of originality, correctness, significance, and ethics compliance—**must be made exclusively by me**, not AI\n  - I bear full responsibility for all judgments, recommendations, and technical claims in my review\n  - I will disclose any AI assistance at the conclusion of my review\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/artefactory/woodtapper](https://github.com/artefactory/woodtapper)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@Abdoulaye-SAKHO) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Scope and significance:** Does this submission demonstrate clear research impact or credible scholarly significance as described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/submitting.html)?\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n### Development history and open-source practice\n\n- [x] **Development timeline:** Does the project show evidence of sustained development over time (preferably months or years) rather than rapid, recent code generation?\n- [x] **Open development:** Was the software developed openly from early stages? For projects with recent public repositories, is there at least six months of public development history with evidence of releases, public issues/pull requests, and ideally external engagement?\n- [x] **Collaborative effort:** Does the commit history show contributions from multiple developers and evidence of iterative refinement through community feedback?\n- [x] **Good practices:** Does the project look like a reusable, non-throwaway research software project that follows good open-source practices (license, documentation, tests and/or verification processes, releases, and clear contribution/support pathways).\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary (required section):** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need (required section):** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field (required section):** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages? If related tools exist, do they provide a clear \"build vs. contribute\" justification explaining their unique scholarly contribution and why alternatives are insufficient?\n- [x] **Software Design (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Software Design\" section that explains the trade-offs weighed, the design/architecture chosen, and why it matters? Is the content compelling and does it demonstrate meaningful design thinking?\n- [x] **Research Impact Statement (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Research Impact Statement\" section providing evidence of realized impact (publications, external use, integrations) or credible near-term significance (benchmarks, reproducible materials, community-readiness signals)? Is the evidence presented compelling?\n- [x] **AI usage disclosure (required section):** Does the paper include an \"AI usage disclosure\" section that transparently discloses any use of generative AI in the software creation, documentation, or paper authoring?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3969572120/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3969615149","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3969615149","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3969615149,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7sm4Ut","user":{"login":"fangzhou-xie","id":45321577,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ1MzIxNTc3","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/45321577?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie","html_url":"https://github.com/fangzhou-xie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fangzhou-xie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T22:31:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T22:31:05Z","body":"Hi @Manishms18, thanks for your interest in reviewing JOSS articles. We already have two reviewers for this submission, and we currently are just waiting for both reviewers to finish their reviews.\n\nI would be happy to invite you to review for future submissions in this area, and you could [register yourself as a reviewer (click the \"Volunteer to review\" on the right)](https://joss.theoj.org/about) to be potentially invited by other editors too. Thanks!","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3969615149/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3969744343","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3969744343","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3969744343,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7snX3X","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T23:02:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T23:02:17Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO I've just begun reviewing this, but it looks good so far.\n\nI've attempted to reproduce the diagrams from the paper, but I'm running into issues. Specifically, I just tried to run https://github.com/artefactory/woodtapper/blob/main/paper/exp_py.ipynb, but I'm hitting an issue with this line:\n\n```python\nos.mkdir('reproduce-exp', exist_ok=True) # create output directory\n```\n\n`exist_ok` doesn't appear to be defined for [os.mkdir](https://docs.python.org/3/library/os.html#os.mkdir). Am I doing something wrong here? Could you check this out on your end and make sure these notebooks are working as expected?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3969744343/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3972145901","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3972145901","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3972145901,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7swiLt","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-27T10:42:26Z","updated_at":"2026-02-27T10:42:26Z","body":"Hello @jncraton ,\n\nThanks again for reviewing our submission.\n\nThe issue came from a change I made from `pathlib.Path.mkdir` to `os.mkdir` to better align with the rest of the codebase, and I didn’t verify it properly afterward. I’ve now updated the code to use `os.makedirs`.\n\nCould you please try reproducing the experiments again? Let me know if you need anything else.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3972145901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3981215675","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3981215675","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3981215675,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7tTIe7","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-01T22:50:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-01T22:50:41Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO Thank you for addressing that. That part of the notebook is working correctly for me now.\n\nWould it be possible to automate dependency installation, including pinning the versions that you used in the paper in these notebooks? That would help with long-term reproducibility.\n\nMy hope would be that I would be able to simply [run these notebooks via colab](https://colab.research.google.com/github/artefactory/woodtapper/blob/main/paper/exp_py.ipynb), but that doesn't work for right now because:\n\n1. `woodtapper` has to be manually installed first. That's relatively simple, but it would be nice to have this dependency automated and tied to the precise version from the paper.\n2. Even with `sklearn` installed, I see `AttributeError: module 'sklearn.tree._utils' has no attribute 'WeightedFenwickTree'` when attempting to run this notebook. I haven't look into this deeply, but it appears that the internals of sklearn may have changed at some point and this needs to be run against a specific version.\n\nThe same basic issue is present in the R notebook. Instructions state that sirus must be installed, but it would be handy if this were automatic and pinned to the version that was used in the paper to prevent any confusion in the future.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3981215675/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3991685840","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3991685840","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3991685840,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7t7ErQ","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-03T15:07:36Z","updated_at":"2026-03-03T15:07:36Z","body":"Hello @jncraton ,\n\nThank you for your feedback. We have updated the repository to address the requested changes. In `paper/README.md`, we now include a link to a Google Colab environment for running the experiments. The notebooks have been updated to be compatible with Colab, and we added clear instructions so users can easily run and test the experiments there.\nThank you as well for suggesting this improvement, which significantly strengthens the reproducibility of our experiments. During this update, we also noticed that installing WoodTapper may require recompilation when `scikit-learn` is already installed. We have therefore updated the main `README.md` with guidelines for this situation.\n\nPlease let us know if anything is not working as expected with the Colab link, or if you have any additional suggestions.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3991685840/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3999133768","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-3999133768","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":3999133768,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7uXfBI","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-04T17:45:44Z","updated_at":"2026-03-04T17:45:44Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO Thank you. I was able to run those notebooks successfully.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/3999133768/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4012847810","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4012847810","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4012847810,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7vLzLC","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-06T16:49:14Z","updated_at":"2026-03-06T16:49:14Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO Is the code to replicate the performance graphs in the paper available? It obviously wouldn't generate identical results due to system differences, but it would still be helpful to replicate the general trend and could be helpful down the line if researchers want to re-run these comparisons against future versions of these tools.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4012847810/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4037670831","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4037670831","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4037670831,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7wqfev","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-11T09:16:31Z","updated_at":"2026-03-11T09:16:31Z","body":"@jncraton — I created a new branch, `dev_abdoulaye`, that contains all the material required to reproduce the computation-time experiments. If everything looks good to you, I will merge it into `main`.\n\n## 1) ExampleBasedExplainability timings\nAll computation-time results for *ExampleBasedExplainability* can be reproduced using the following notebooks:\n- `paper/timing/timing-skgrf.ipynb`\n- `paper/timing/timing-exampleSampling-with-skgrf-plot.ipynb`\n\n**Note:** these `skgrf`-based notebooks cannot be executed on Google Colab, because `skgrf` cannot be installed there.\n\n## 2) ExtractionRules timings \nYou can now reproduce the experiments from the paper that compare the runtime of the three SIRUS implementations: **R**, **Julia**, and **Python (ours)**.\n\nSince each implementation has its own dependencies, you will need to set up a separate environment for each one; the setup procedure is described in `paper/timing/README.md`.\n\n\n\nThe provided scripts report **only the total runtime** (forest training + rule extraction). The runtimes of the two intermediate steps—(i) growing the forest and (ii) extracting the rules—are **not measured dynamically** by the scripts; instead, they are **hard-coded** in the `.csv` files under `time-csv/`.\n\nThis is because, for the R implementation, we patched the source code (see `R/Sirus.R`, starting at line 172 in the upstream [SIRUS repository](https://gitlab.com/drti/sirus/-/tree/master?ref_type=heads)) to print both the forest-growing time and the rule-extraction time, installed this patched version in our R environment, saved the console output to a `.txt` log, and then parsed these logs to populate the `.csv` files. We followed the same workflow for the Julia implementation.\n\n\n\nTo facilitate benchmarking on your own setup, we provide a configuration that recomputes **only the total fitting time** and updates the corresponding `.csv` files accordingly. In addition, `paper/timing/README.md` includes guidance on how to patch the R/Julia sources to re-enable the step-wise breakdown (forest growth vs. rule extraction). If you do so on your side, you can regenerate those values and update the relevant `.csv` files to plot your own forest-growing and rule-extraction times.\n\nThe step-wise breakdown is included in the paper mainly for pedagogical clarity; the primary metric of interest remains the **total runtime**.\n\nWould these additions address your concern? We tried to strike the best trade-off between reproducibility and implementation constraints.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4037670831/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4055700684","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4055700684","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4055700684,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7xvRTM","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-13T14:47:13Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T14:47:13Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO As I'm going through the checklist for the paper, I noticed that it doesn't have a separate \"Summary\" section as required. It might be nice for readers if something like the second paragraph in the current \"Statement of need\" section were pulled up as a \"Summary\" section right at the beginning.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4055700684/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4055817365","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4055817365","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4055817365,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7xvtyV","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-13T15:01:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T15:01:59Z","body":"@jncraton - Indeed, there is no “Summary” section because we thought it was no longer required under the updated guidelines (and it was not flagged by the compilation bot). However, as you suggested, we have moved the second paragraph of the current “Statement of need” section to the beginning of the paper and presented it as a dedicated “Summary” section.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4055817365/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.gi