sues/10112","id":4056024189,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7xwgR9","user":{"login":"jncraton","id":103612,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMzYxMg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103612?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton","html_url":"https://github.com/jncraton","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jncraton/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-13T15:30:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T15:30:57Z","body":"@Abdoulaye-SAKHO \n\n> There is no “Summary” section because we thought it was no longer required under the updated guidelines (and it was not flagged by the compilation bot)\n\nI noticed that as well. It sounds like you may have a better understanding of the current guidelines than I do. I only mentioned the summary section because it was listed as required in the checklist. If this is no longer required and you prefer your previous paper structure, I'm quite happy with that.\n\nOverall, I think this project and paper look good. Thank you for your time building, maintaining, and updating this as well as your time writing it up and formalizing your results.\n\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4056024189/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4056063982","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4056063982","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4056063982,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7xwp_u","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-13T15:37:01Z","updated_at":"2026-03-13T15:37:01Z","body":"@jncraton Thank you very much for taking the time to review our submission and for your constructive feedback !","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4056063982/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4099560223","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4099560223","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4099560223,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs70WlMf","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-20T16:52:59Z","updated_at":"2026-03-20T16:52:59Z","body":"Hello, thank you to the reviewers for their time and thoughtful feedback on our submission. Please let us know if there is anything we can do on our side to help move the process forward.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4099560223/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4151107436","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4151107436","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4151107436,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs73bN9s","user":{"login":"jungtaekkim","id":20551631,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTUxNjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20551631?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim","html_url":"https://github.com/jungtaekkim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-29T21:16:05Z","updated_at":"2026-05-02T14:27:05Z","body":"## Review checklist for @jungtaekkim\n\n### AI usage\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS AI policy](https://joss.theoj.org/about#ai-policy) and understand that:\n  - AI may only be used for **non-substantive assistance** (e.g., grammar checking my review text, contextualizing public materials)\n  - **All evaluative decisions**—including scoring, accept/reject recommendations, and assessments of originality, correctness, significance, and ethics compliance—**must be made exclusively by me**, not AI\n  - I bear full responsibility for all judgments, recommendations, and technical claims in my review\n  - I will disclose any AI assistance at the conclusion of my review\n\n### Conflict of interest\n\n- [x] I confirm that I have read the [JOSS conflict of interest (COI) policy](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/COI.md) and that: I have no COIs with reviewing this work or that any perceived COIs have been waived by JOSS for the purpose of this review.\n\n### Code of Conduct\n\n- [x] I confirm that I read and will adhere to the [JOSS code of conduct](https://github.com/openjournals/joss/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n\n### General checks\n\n- [x] **Repository:** Is the source code for this software available at the [https://github.com/artefactory/woodtapper](https://github.com/artefactory/woodtapper)?\n- [x] **License:** Does the repository contain a plain-text LICENSE or COPYING file with the contents of an [OSI approved](https://opensource.org/licenses/alphabetical) software license?\n- [x] **Contribution and authorship:** Has the submitting author (@Abdoulaye-SAKHO) made major contributions to the software? Does the full list of paper authors seem appropriate and complete?\n- [x] **Scope and significance:** Does this submission demonstrate clear research impact or credible scholarly significance as described in the [JOSS guidelines](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/submitting.html)?\n- [x] **Data sharing:** If the paper contains original data, data are accessible to the reviewers. If the paper contains no original data, please check this item.\n- [x] **Reproducibility:** If the paper contains original results, results are entirely reproducible by reviewers. If the paper contains no original results, please check this item.\n- [x] **Human and animal research:** If the paper contains original data research on humans subjects or animals, does it comply with [JOSS's human participants research policy and/or animal research policy](https://joss.readthedocs.io/en/latest/policies.html?highlight=animal#joss-policies)? If the paper contains no such data, please check this item.\n\n### Development history and open-source practice\n\n- [x] **Development timeline:** Does the project show evidence of sustained development over time (preferably months or years) rather than rapid, recent code generation?\n- [x] **Open development:** Was the software developed openly from early stages? For projects with recent public repositories, is there at least six months of public development history with evidence of releases, public issues/pull requests, and ideally external engagement?\n- [x] **Collaborative effort:** Does the project show evidence of community engagement such as contributions from multiple developers, issues/discussions from external users, or community influence on the development described in the paper?\n- [x] **Good practices:** Does the project look like a reusable, non-throwaway research software project that follows good open-source practices (license, documentation, tests and/or verification processes, releases, and clear contribution/support pathways).\n\n### Functionality\n\n- [x] **Installation:** Does installation proceed as outlined in the documentation?\n- [x] **Functionality:** Have the functional claims of the software been confirmed?\n- [x] **Performance:** If there are any performance claims of the software, have they been confirmed? (If there are no claims, please check off this item.)\n\n### Documentation\n\n- [x] **A statement of need**: Do the authors clearly state what problems the software is designed to solve and who the target audience is?\n- [x] **Installation instructions:** Is there a clearly-stated list of dependencies? Ideally these should be handled with an automated package management solution.\n- [x] **Example usage:** Do the authors include examples of how to use the software (ideally to solve real-world analysis problems).\n- [x] **Functionality documentation:** Is the core functionality of the software documented to a satisfactory level (e.g., API method documentation)?\n- [x] **Automated tests:** Are there automated tests or manual steps described so that the functionality of the software can be verified?\n- [x] **Community guidelines:** Are there clear guidelines for third parties wishing to 1. Contribute to the software 2. Report issues or problems with the software 3. Seek support\n\n### Software paper\n\n- [x] **Summary (required section):** Has a clear description of the high-level functionality and purpose of the software for a diverse, non-specialist audience been provided?\n- [x] **A statement of need (required section):** Does the paper have a section titled 'Statement of need' that clearly states what problems the software is designed to solve, who the target audience is, and its relation to other work?\n- [x] **State of the field (required section):** Do the authors describe how this software compares to other commonly-used packages? If related tools exist, do they provide a clear \"build vs. contribute\" justification explaining their unique scholarly contribution and why alternatives are insufficient?\n- [x] **Software Design (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Software Design\" section that explains the trade-offs weighed, the design/architecture chosen, and why it matters? Is the content compelling and does it demonstrate meaningful design thinking?\n- [x] **Research Impact Statement (required section):** Does the paper include a \"Research Impact Statement\" section providing evidence of realized impact (publications, external use, integrations) or credible near-term significance (benchmarks, reproducible materials, community-readiness signals)? Is the evidence presented compelling?\n- [x] **AI usage disclosure (required section):** Does the paper include an \"AI usage disclosure\" section that transparently discloses any use of generative AI in the software creation, documentation, or paper authoring?\n- [x] **Quality of writing:** Is the paper well written (i.e., it does not require editing for structure, language, or writing quality)?\n- [x] **References:** Is the list of references complete, and is everything cited appropriately that should be cited (e.g., papers, datasets, software)? Do references in the text use the proper [citation syntax](https://pandoc.org/MANUAL.html#extension-citations)?\n","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4151107436/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4268096926","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4268096926","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4268096926,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7-Zf2e","user":{"login":"Abdoulaye-SAKHO","id":130471399,"node_id":"U_kgDOB8bV5w","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/130471399?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","html_url":"https://github.com/Abdoulaye-SAKHO","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Abdoulaye-SAKHO/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T12:48:05Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T12:48:05Z","body":"@editorialbot commands","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4268096926/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4268097302","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4268097302","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4268097302,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs7-Zf8W","user":{"login":"editorialbot","id":89919391,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjg5OTE5Mzkx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/89919391?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot","html_url":"https://github.com/editorialbot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/editorialbot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-17T12:48:09Z","updated_at":"2026-04-17T12:48:09Z","body":"\nHello @Abdoulaye-SAKHO, here are the things you can ask me to do:\n\n```\n\n# List all available commands\n@editorialbot commands\n\n# Get a list of all editors's GitHub handles\n@editorialbot list editors\n\n# Adds a checklist for the reviewer using this command\n@editorialbot generate my checklist\n\n# Set a value for branch\n@editorialbot set joss-paper as branch\n\n# Run checks and provide information on the repository and the paper file\n@editorialbot check repository\n\n# Check the references of the paper for missing DOIs\n@editorialbot check references\n\n# Generates the pdf paper\n@editorialbot generate pdf\n\n# Generates a LaTeX preprint file\n@editorialbot generate preprint\n\n# Get a link to the complete list of reviewers\n@editorialbot list reviewers\n\n```\n","author_association":"COLLABORATOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4268097302/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/comments/4323102581","html_url":"https://github.com/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112#issuecomment-4323102581","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/openjournals/joss-reviews/issues/10112","id":4323102581,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAx6EUs8AAAABAa1PdQ","user":{"login":"jungtaekkim","id":20551631,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIwNTUxNjMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/20551631?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim","html_url":"https://github.com/jungtaekkim","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jungtaekkim/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-26T22:00:51Z","updated_at":"2026-04-26T22:00:51Z","body":"@editorialbot generate pdf","author_association":"NONE"